"ec"],["hs","ws"],["nt","Since North-South have 8 clubs and only 7 spades between them, the @CQ is more likely to drop doubleton than the @SQ. "],["pg",""],["ls","ns"],["ls","ss"],["ls","ec"],["ls","ws"],["md","0,s6cq,,sqc6"],["at","South should therefore start by cashing the top clubs. "],["pg",""],["ls","nc"],["at","Furthermore, it is correct to cash the @CA first "],["pg",""],["ls","sc"],["pc","ca"],["pc","c"],["pc","c"],["pc","c"],["pg",""],["pc","c"],["pc","c"],["pc","ck"],["pc","c"],["pg",""],["hs","ns"],["hs","ss"],["hs","wc"],["at","so that the lead will be in the dummy (to finesse in spades) should the @CQ remain outstanding. "],["pg",""],["ls","wc"],["ls","ns"],["ls","ss"],["pc","s"],["pc","s"],["pc","sj"],["pc","s"],["pg",""],["hs","nh"],["hs","sh"],["at","When the spade finesse wins, South can cross to the dummy in hearts, "],["pg",""],["ls","nh"],["ls","sh"],["pc","h"],["pc","h"],["pc","hk"],["pc","h"],["pg",""],["hs","nh"],["at","cash dummy's other top heart, "],["pg",""],["ls","nh"],["pc","ha"],["pc","h"],["pc","c"],["pc","h"],["pg",""],["hs","ns"],["hs","ss"],["at","and repeat the spade finesse."],["pg",""],["up","16"],["md","0,sqhq,,s67"],["ls","ns"],["hs","ws"],["nt","Note that it would be a mistake to cash a top spade early in an attempt to guard against a singleton @SQ with West. The odds of West holding a singleton @SQ "],["pg",""],["ls","ws"],["hs","es"],["md","0,s67,,hqsq"],["at","are much less than the odds of East holding 4 or more spades to the @SQ. Laying down a top spade before crossing to the @CK would be fatal in the above layout."],["",""]]}}